        "summary":  "Damodaran argues that venture capital\u0027s structural incentives — pricing companies by comparables rather than intrinsic value, and chasing power-law returns — systematically bias founders and VCs toward revenue scaling at the expense of profitable business models. He identifies six factors that determine true scalability (market size, growth, industry structure, capital intensity, customer inertia, and key-person dependency) and maps eight outcome scenarios from best-case \u0027Lightning in a Bottle\u0027 to worst-case \u0027Cut Your Losses.\u0027 He contends that changes in capital markets — longer private-company lifespans, public equity funding of private firms — have removed the historical discipline of IPO scrutiny, producing \u0027big and broken\u0027 businesses with sky-high valuations built on questionable economics.",
