                                                              "summary":  "Brown profiles Ron Baron\u0027s decades-long track record of identifying and holding unconventional, visionary investments ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â most notably Tesla, purchased at $14/share in 2014, and a large position in SpaceX. Baron\u0027s strategy involves taking concentrated positions in companies with long-duration growth runways and holding through extreme volatility rather than following the restrictive mandates typical of institutional funds. This willingness to ignore mainstream skepticism and stay the course is presented as the core explanation for Baron\u0027s consistent outperformance versus both indices and peers.",
